Adopt teammate's VSP-rubric axis-scoring model, validated exactly against their ground-truth dataset (540/540 axis scores, 60/60 Founder Scores match).

Replaces the source-weighted (45/25/15/15) Founder Score aggregator with:
- component_map.py: 19 components -> axis/vsp_code/weight, copied from their component_map.csv
- axis_engine.py: score_axis() reproducing quality = strength x (0.55+0.45*confidence),
  weighted mean by component weight, plus coverage_pct and trend
- founder_score.py: founder_score = min(99, round(axis*0.75 + prior_ventures*9 + shipped_artifacts*3))
- ingestion/claims.py: translates GitHub/Scholar/LinkedIn sub-scores into component-tagged
  Claim rows instead of a standalone per-source composite
- pipeline.py: fills explicit 'unobserved' claims for uncovered Founder components so
  coverage_pct honestly reflects partial evidence rather than reading artificially high

Schema: Claim gains axis/component/vsp_code/strength_0_100/evidence_state/
verification_count/contradicts_claim_id/observed_at; Founder gains prior_ventures.
